---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import MarkdownFormatter from '../../components/MarkdownFormatter.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Markdown to AI-Prompt Formatter"
  description="Strip Markdown formatting into clean plain text, or wrap it in XML tags — ideal for pasting documents into an AI prompt."
>
  <MarkdownFormatter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why reformat Markdown before prompting</h2>
  <p>
    Pasting raw Markdown (headers, bullets, bold syntax) into a prompt adds
    noise that can distract a model from the actual content. Stripping it to
    plain text, or wrapping it in clear XML tags, gives the model a cleaner
    signal — especially useful for long documents or structured notes.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your Markdown content.</li>
    <li>Choose "Plain text" for a clean, formatting-free version, or "XML-wrapped" for models that respond well to tagged structure (like Claude).</li>
    <li>Copy and paste directly into your prompt.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Markdown to AI-Prompt FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why would I want XML tags?</strong> Some models, particularly
    Claude, are trained to pay close attention to XML-style structure,
    making it easier for the model to distinguish your instructions from
    the document content.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
